{"name":"Highlighter Turquoise","hex":"#009e6c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"highlighter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A marker pen used to highlight text.","A cosmetic product that reflects light, used to emphasize the contours of the face etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/highlighter"},{"term":"turquoise","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sky-blue, greenish-blue, or greenish-gray semi-precious gemstone.","A pale greenish-blue colour, like that of the gemstone."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of turquoise (the gemstone).","Having a pale greenish-blue colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/turquoise"}],"entries":[{"title":"Highlighter","blocks":[{"text":"A highlighter, also called a fluorescent pen, is a type of writing device used to bring attention to sections of text by marking them with a vivid, translucent colour.\nA typical highlighter is fluorescent yellow, with the colour coming from pyranine. Different compounds, such as rhodamines are used for other colours."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Highlighter","wikidata":"Q559350"},{"title":"Turquoise","blocks":[{"text":"Turquoise is an opaque, blue-to-green mineral that is a hydrous phosphate of copper and aluminium, with the chemical formula CuAl6(PO4)4(OH)8·4H2O. It is rare and valuable in finer grades and has been prized as a gemstone for millennia due to its hue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Turquoise-40031.jpg/330px-Turquoise-40031.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turquoise","wikidata":"Q165254"},{"title":"Turquoise (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Turquoise is a cyan color, based on the mineral of the same name."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turquoise_(color)","wikidata":"Q5960345"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Markee